close_reason: "Delivered MCP 2026-07-28 subscription and transport contracts with public SDK primitives, stdio and Streamable HTTP adapters, security/backpressure semantics, package publication surface, docs, installed-consumer proof, and exact 100% coverage."
body: "## Streaming model\n\n- subscriptions/listen is one long-lived POST-response stream with explicit requested notification types and a server-minted subscription identifier.\n- tools, prompts, resources, and resource-subscription changes flow only through the opted-in listen stream.\n- progress and message notifications remain on the response stream of their originating request.\n- A broken request stream loses that in-flight request and the client retries with a new JSON-RPC request id.\n- STDIO and Streamable HTTP share SDK handlers, cancellation, ordering, backpressure, heartbeat policy, and structured failures.\n- Streamable HTTP validates Mcp-Method and Mcp-Name and supports declared x-mcp-header parameter mappings without header injection."
